Storyteller's Toolkit: Pixel Art - Lily
Author: Two Orcs

Applies to the Lily character assets used by TRUEOS as Lilly, including
tools/Lilly.tar.lz4 and the source asset pack at ../Lilly/.

Source: https://two-orcs.itch.io/storytellers-toolkit-pixel-art-lily
Terms retrieved: 2026-11-10
Purchase confirmed by the TRUEOS project owner on 2026-11-10.

Upstream license terms (transcribed from the product page):

You may

Use the assets in commercial and non-commercial projects (games, visual novels, apps, videos, streams, trailers, promotional art).

Modify the assets (edit, recolor, resize, crop, animate, convert formats) for use in your project.

Use the assets in multiple projects, as long as you/your team are the end user(s) of the files.

You may not

Resell, redistribute, re-upload, share, or gift the assets (including modified versions) as standalone files or as part of another asset pack, bundle, template, or “starter project.”

Mint/sell the assets (or close derivatives) as NFTs, tokens, or on marketplaces that primarily trade standalone assets.

Use the assets to train, fine-tune, or build datasets for machine learning / generative models, or offer them in an AI image generation dataset.

Claim the assets as your own or remove copyright notices.

Team use

The assets can be used by a single person or a single team/studio working on the same project(s).

Contractors may use the assets only while working on your project and must delete the source files when finished.

If you want a license for multiple studios/clients, contact me for an extended license.
